course: dictionary
lesson: 9926
title: Tankful: the amount a tank holds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tankful is the amount a tank can hold when it is full. The word tank is the container, and tankful tells you how much fills it completely. «A tankful of petrol» means petrol filling the whole tank.
explain: Use the words around tankful to find its meaning. «A battery does not hold a tankful of electricity: it holds chemicals that push electricity round the loop.» The sentence says a battery is not a tank, so it cannot hold a tankful. The clue is the word tank: a tankful is what a tank holds.
explain: Maths problems use tankful as a measure. «A tankful of petrol is 50 litres; the car goes 600 km on one tankful.» The numbers near the word tell you how much a full tank holds and how far it takes the car.
fact: A tankful is the amount a tank can hold when it is full.
fact: Tankful is a noun. You can say a tankful, or two tankfuls.
fact: You can say a tankful of petrol, a tankful of water, or fill a tankful.
fact: «A battery does not hold a tankful of electricity» shows that tankful is used for what a tank holds, not for batteries.
fact: In maths, a tankful is a measure, so it can appear in number problems.
exercise: «A battery does not hold a tankful of electricity.» What does tankful mean? | A type of electric wire | A small pocket of air | *The amount a tank can hold when it is full | The end of a long journey
exercise: Dad says, «We need a tankful of petrol for the trip.» What is a tankful here? | An empty tank at the garage | *The amount of petrol that fills the whole tank | A petrol station on the motorway | A cup of tea for the road
exercise: Nadia says «one tankful» means one small sip of water. Is she right? | No, it means an empty tank | Yes, it means a tiny cup | *No, it means the whole amount a tank holds when it is full | Yes, a tankful is a small sip
test: The fish tank holds 40 litres when full. What is the tankful of water? | *The whole 40 litres that fills the tank | A bucket that is empty | The fish swimming inside | Just one litre of water
test: «The car goes 600 km on one tankful.» What does one tankful mean in this sentence? | Half a tank of petrol | A short walk to school | A map of the road | *The full amount of petrol the tank holds
exam: Which sentence uses tankful correctly? | The tankful sang a song in the rain | She ate a tankful of cake for lunch | A tankful is a loud shout across the field | *We filled the car with a tankful of petrol
